{"ref":"BDB, נִינְוֵה","hw":"נִינְוֵה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">נִינְוֵה</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.loc. Nineveh</strong>, capital of Assyria <strong>(</strong>Assyrian <em>Ninâ, Ninua, Ninû</em>, cf. Schr<sup> COT Gloss.</sup> Dl<sup>Par260</sup><strong>)</strong>;—<a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:11\" href=\"/Genesis.10.11\">Gn 10:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:12\" href=\"/Genesis.10.12\">12</a> (J), <a data-ref=\"II Kings 19:36\" href=\"/II_Kings.19.36\">2 K 19:36</a> = <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 37:37\" href=\"/Isaiah.37.37\">Is 37:37</a>, <a data-ref=\"Nahum 1:1\" href=\"/Nahum.1.1\">Na 1:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nahum 2:9\" href=\"/Nahum.2.9\">2:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nahum 3:7\" href=\"/Nahum.3.7\">3:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Zephaniah 2:13\" href=\"/Zephaniah.2.13\">Zp 2:13</a> <a data-ref=\"Jonah 1:2\" href=\"/Jonah.1.2\">Jon 1:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:3\" href=\"/Jonah.3.3\">3:3a</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:4\" href=\"/Jonah.3.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:5\" href=\"/Jonah.3.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:6\" href=\"/Jonah.3.6\">6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:7\" href=\"/Jonah.3.7\">7</a>, called <span dir=\"rtl\">הָעִיר הַגְּדוֹלָה</span> v <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:3\" href=\"/Jonah.3.3\">3b</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jonah 4:11\" href=\"/Jonah.4.11\">4:11</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:4\" href=\"/Jonah.3.4\">3:4f.</a>); 𝔊 Νινευη, 𝔊L Νινευι. Site on E. bank of Tigris marked by mounds <em>Neby Yunus</em> and <em>Kuyundjik</em>, opposite Mosul. Cf. Layard <sup>Nineveh and its Remains, 1848; Monuments of N. 1849 f.</sup> Billerbeck u. Jeremias<sup> BAS iii. 1 (1895), 107 ff.</sup>","next":"BDB, נִינָס","prev":"BDB, נִין²"}